{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into sensing and motion capability so the supervisor can react to uncontrollable obstacle observations before issuing one-shot open-loop motion pulses. The specifications encode a conservative but coverage-biased policy: random_walk is the default in clear exploration, short forward progress is used after clear confirmation, obstacle events always force dedicated turn recovery, and full_rotate is reserved for a last-resort blocked state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model perception as uncontrollable environment updates and motion as controllable one-shot actions.",
    "Use small deterministic specifications for clear exploration, short forward progress, left/right/front obstacle recovery, and a rare full-scan escape."
  ],
